Subject: [PATCH 6/6] zle: leave a host's answer to a terminal query out of the keys

A program that asks the terminal something and ends before it reads the answer, or never reads
it, leaves the host's answer in the terminal's input, and the line editor finds it at its prompt.
ZLE decodes it as keys: an unbound sequence beeps and the rest of the answer is typed into the
line. The reader takes the answer out at the one place the editor reads the first byte of a key,
before the key lookup sees it: when the byte is an Escape and the terminal has already delivered
the rest of an answer the host's query broker builds, the whole answer is taken and dropped;
anything else is given back to the key lookup untouched and in order. Nothing waits for a byte
the terminal has not delivered, so no key a person presses is held back. A `read -k` in a widget
never goes through this read, and `vared`, `select`, a quoted insertion and a bracketed paste are
left alone.

This patch is a derivative work of Zsh and carries the Zsh licence; see shells/zsh/LICENSE.

--- a/Src/Zle/zle.mdd
+++ b/Src/Zle/zle.mdd
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 zle_misc.o zle_move.o zle_params.o zle_refresh.o \
 zle_thingy.o zle_tricky.o zle_utils.o zle_vi.o zle_word.o \
 textobjects.o kr_bridge.o kr_bridge_cbor.o kr_bridge_crypto.o \
-kr_bridge_zle.o"
+kr_bridge_reply.o kr_bridge_zle.o"
 
 headers="zle.h zle_things.h"
 
--- a/Src/Zle/zle_keymap.c
+++ b/Src/Zle/zle_keymap.c
@@ -28,6 +28,9 @@
  */
 
 #include "zle.mdh"
+
+#include "kr_bridge.h"
+#include "kr_bridge_zle.h"
 
 /*
  * Keymap structures:
@@ -1693,7 +1696,15 @@
 static int
 getkeybuf(int w)
 {
-    int c = getbyte((long)w, NULL, 1);
+    int c;
+
+    /*
+     * A host's answer to a terminal query is no key: when an Escape begins one, the reader takes
+     * the whole answer here and reads on.
+     */
+    do {
+	c = getbyte((long)w, NULL, 1);
+    } while (c == '\033' && kr_zle_host_reply_dropped());
 
     if(c < 0)
 	return EOF;
